<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog https://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.23.xsd">
    <!--
      Karma stops being a stored score and becomes a derived one:
      10 - (abandons in the last 30 days), floor 0, recomputed on every read.
      That turns two reads that used to be a single-row lookup into counting
      queries, so they get their indexes here.

      game_reliability_events already has
      idx_game_reliability_events_user_time (user_uid, occurred_at) from
      2026-09-18 — exactly the shape the window count needs, so nothing is
      added for it; this comment exists so the next reader does not go looking.

      game_result_players has idx_game_result_players_uid (uid) from
      2026-09-08-game-stats, but the window count also has to reach
      game_results.played_at for every one of those rows. An index on
      played_at makes the other side of that join a range scan instead of a
      sequential read once the table grows.

      No column changes: user_profiles.game_karma and
      game_completed_since_recovery are deliberately LEFT IN PLACE, unread and
      unwritten (see UserProfile's field comments). Dropping them would be an
      irreversible migration in exchange for nothing.
    -->
    <changeSet id="2026-09-21-game-reliability-window-index" author="mrodek">
        <createIndex tableName="game_results" indexName="idx_game_results_played_at">
            <column name="played_at"/>
        </createIndex>
        <rollback>
            <dropIndex tableName="game_results" indexName="idx_game_results_played_at"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
